# Line endings, written by Pave Studio when it created this project.
#
# Without this file, git stores whatever bytes each contributor's
# core.autocrlf produced. A Windows contributor with core.autocrlf=true
# commits CRLF; a macOS contributor commits LF; each then sees the
# other's files as entirely changed.
#
# text=auto: git stores text as LF and leaves binaries alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts stop running if they are checked out with LF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never normalise vendored dependencies: keep them byte-for-byte as
# published. Last, so it wins over the "*" rule above.
**/node_modules/** -text
